368: obligation for gate-passed discovery genomes.  At lines 248--255, it states that
369: candidates supplying only a statement locus or only legal theorem code do not
370: pass the discovery gate as theorem genomes.  At lines 258--267 and 269--278, it
371: states that mechanical expansion and same-classifier genome compression do not
372: imply discovery.  At lines 280--297, it states that a discovery transition
373: supplies a semantic naming certificate and a ledger witness.  At lines 299--332,
374: it records the positive-discovery, public-weight, and gate-kind-soundness
375: interfaces used by the package verifier below.  At lines 334--345, it states
376: that gate demotion leaves a claim kind no stronger than its actual evidence.  At
377: lines 366--374, it states that lineage-consistent accepted claims form an
378: auditable acyclic lineage graph.  At lines 393--418, it states that the lowest
379: score need not be the best target and that, when all other discovery-potential
380: coordinates are fixed, a positive classifier-change coefficient makes the
381: selection operator favor the classifier-changing candidate.  At lines 432--439,
382: it states that an accepted pipeline has no accepted discovery claim missing gate
383: evidence.  At lines 441--455, pipeline safety states that accepted discovery
384: claims have classifier change, semantic naming certificate, ledger witness,
385: DNA-complete theorem genome, score certificate, lineage witness, and an explicit
386: not-claimed boundary.  At lines 457--485, the main pipeline theorem and principle
387: separate record growth, score reduction, recombination, classifier change,
388: ledgered discovery, and certified structural theorem-genome change.  These paraphrases are
389: used only as a stable interface to the pinned source theorem spine; no stronger
390: source rebuild claim is made here.
