529: \end{proposition}
530: 
531: \begin{proof}
532: Lemma~\ref{lem:source-interface-extraction-correctness} proves that the only
533: imported source labels used by the paper are the sixteen rows of
534: Table~\ref{tab:source-interface-record}, each with a fixed line range and bounded
535: summary.  The paragraph preceding that lemma fixes the original local source
536: path, source commit, extraction date, and JSON mirror.  The supplemental copy is
537: a file-level snapshot of the same source-interface document, named by the same
538: commit hash.  Therefore a reviewer does not need access to the author's absolute
539: path in order to inspect the imported interface: the table gives the labels and
540: line ranges, the JSON record gives the machine-readable binding, and the bundle
541: copy gives the text snapshot against which those ranges are checked.  The current reviewer-facing distribution mode is fixed by the proposition:
542: the bundle is uploadable supplemental material, not an unrecorded private
