606: 
607: \begin{proposition}[Source-interface evidence-level separation]
608: \label{prop:source-interface-evidence-level-separation}
609: Let $r$ be any accepted manuscript claim whose discovery component cites one of
610: the imported labels in Table~\ref{tab:source-interface-record}.  If $r$ uses only
611: Lemma~\ref{lem:source-interface-extraction-correctness}, then the imported-label
612: premise of $r$ is accepted only at the manual path-verified bounded-paraphrase
613: level.  If $r$ additionally cites
614: Proposition~\ref{prop:source-interface-record-file-consistency}, then the same
615: premise is upgraded only by the finite record comparisons listed in that
616: proposition: table--JSON equality, manifest agreement, snapshot digest and line
617: count agreement, and label containment in the declared ranges.  In neither case
618: does the premise become a fresh Lean/BEDC rebuild, a proof of the semantic truth
619: of the imported source theorem, or an unbounded restatement of the source text.
620: Consequently the finite-record interface theorem, Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}, can use the imported
621: discovery-gate spine only through these two explicitly separated evidence
622: levels.
623: \end{proposition}
624: 
625: \begin{proof}
626: The operational evidence level of a cited source-interface premise is determined
627: by the record fields actually available for that premise.  Lemma~\ref{lem:source-interface-extraction-correctness}
628: supplies a pinned path, commit, extraction date, label, line range, and bounded
629: summary for each of the ten imported labels, and its proof states that no later
630: use may exceed that bounded summary.  Therefore a claim using only the lemma has
631: exactly the manual path-verified bounded-paraphrase evidence listed there.
632: 
633: Proposition~\ref{prop:source-interface-record-file-consistency} adds a different
634: finite record: the verifier parses the manuscript table, the JSON mirror, the
635: manifest's pinned-source-snapshot record, and the bundled source snapshot, and it
636: checks the six finite conditions enumerated in its proof.  Those checks upgrade
637: the source-interface premise only with respect to record-file consistency and
638: range containment.  The same proposition expressly excludes semantic truth of
639: the imported theorems and preserves the bounded-paraphrase restriction.  No row
640: in Table~\ref{tab:source-interface-record}, no field of
641: \path{source_interface_record.json}, and no command-boundary row records a fresh
